Z||000000||Richard Parnell||12-04-2000||06:18 PM||||Still haven't gotten my speedo to work since the conversion.  First it read a constant 50 mph (stopped or moving) now it's at a constant 20 mph.  I pulled the connector at the tranny and loosened the screw honding the gear unit in.  When I tried to lift the unit out it doesn't seen to be big enough to come through the hole in the tranny.  I seem to remember being able to remove the entire unit to check the fluid before.  Also when I put everything back together it doesn't seem to seat down inot anything.  Any ides about the prob.  My car is an 87 SC with 5 speed Isuzu.||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||12-05-2000||08:48 AM||||Pretty sure the VSS is supposed to pull out (I know least about the Isuzu trans., though).<P>Since you say you can't get the VSS out... Guess I might try plugging a known good VSS (from another car) into the harness, turn the ignition on, and run the VSS with a variable-speed drill or something.  Obviously, if the speedo runs that way, trouble is in the (original) VSS or trans.  Else, the trouble's in the car (gage/wiring).<P>Might want to check the IP connectors.   ||||reg||3
Z||000002||Richard Parnell||12-05-2000||01:03 PM||||Thanks Stu.  IP connectors?||||reg||5
Z||000003||StuGood||12-05-2000||01:13 PM||||IP = Instrument panel.  I meant the dash connectors.  One for the speedo plugs into bottom of LHS of the dash; it's accessible by removing the lower cover panel.<P>Might want to check the 2 connectors that plug into the back of the gage cluster, too.  (not sure if they affect the speedo).||||reg||1
